message.content:
I need to restructure Rankora's navigation to separate Dashboard (overview) from My Jobs (management). This is a multi-file refactor.

## ARCHITECTURE RULES
- Use ONLY shadcn-ui components from `src/components/ui/`
- Import with `@/` prefix
- Use Tailwind CSS only, Lucide icons, `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`
- Single Supabase client from `@/integrations/supabase/client`
- Sonner toasts for notifications

## CHANGES NEEDED

### 1. Create `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Rankora/src/pages/MyJobs.tsx`

A new full page that wraps the existing `JobsOverviewCard` with the same layout shell (AppHeader, Sidebar). This page is the "full management" view.

The page should:
- Use the same `SidebarProvider` + `JobSidebar` + `SidebarInset` layout as Index.tsx
- Include `AppHeader`
- Show a page header: "My Jobs" title + "Manage all your job postings" subtitle + "Create Job" button (right-aligned)
- Render the existing `JobsOverviewCard` component with full search/filter/sort/pagination
- When a job row is clicked, navigate to `/` and load that job (use a URL param or state)

IMPORTANT: The MyJobs page needs access to the same `pastJobs` data and sidebar functionality. Since Index.tsx currently owns all that state, the cleanest approach is:

- MyJobs fetches its own jobs data (same query as Index.tsx fetchPastJobs)
- When a job is clicked in JobsOverviewCard, navigate to `/?job={jobId}` 
- Index.tsx should check for `job` URL param on mount and auto-select that job

Here's the page structure:

```tsx
import { useState, useCallback, useEffect } from "react";
import { useAuth } from "@/hooks/useAuth";
import { useNavigate } from "react-router-dom";
import { supabase } from "@/integrations/supabase/client";
import AppHeader from "@/components/AppHeader";
import JobsOverviewCard from "@/components/JobsOverviewCard";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Plus } from "lucide-react";
import { toast } from "sonner";
import type { PastJob } from "@/pages/Index";

const MyJobs = () => {
  const { user } = useAuth();
  const navigate = useNavigate();
  const [jobs, setJobs] = useState<PastJob[]>([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  // Fetch jobs
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!user) return;
    setLoading(true);
    supabase
      .from("jobs")
      .select("id, title, job_description, status, created_at, jd_analysis_json, dynamic_weights_json, inbox_email, resumes(count)")
      .eq("user_id", user.id)
      .order("created_at", { ascending: false })
      .limit(100)
      .then(({ data }) => {
        if (data) {
          setJobs(data.map((j: any) => ({
            id: j.id,
            title: j.title,
            job_description: j.job_description,
            status: j.status,
            created_at: j.created_at,
            resume_count: j.resumes?.[0]?.count ?? 0,
            jd_analysis_json: j.jd_analysis_json,
            dynamic_weights_json: j.dynamic_weights_json,
            inbox_email: j.inbox_email ?? null,
          })));
        }
      })
      .catch(() => toast.error("Failed to load jobs"))
      .finally(() => setLoading(false));
  }, [user]);

  const handleSelectJob = (jobId: string) => {
    navigate(`/?job=${jobId}`);
  };

  const handleCreateJob = () => {
    navigate("/?new=1");
  };

  return (
    <div className="min-h-svh bg-background">
      <AppHeader />
      <div className="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 space-y-6">
        {/* Page header */}
        <div className="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4">
          <div>
            <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold text-foreground">My Jobs</h1>
            <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1">Manage all your job postings.</p>
          </div>
          <Button size="lg" className="gap-2 shadow-md px-6" onClick={handleCreateJob}>
            <Plus className="h-4 w-4" /> Create Job
          </Button>
        </div>

        {/* Full jobs table */}
        <JobsOverviewCard jobs={jobs} loading={loading} onSelectJob={handleSelectJob} />
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};

export default MyJobs;
```

### 2. Modify `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Rankora/src/App.tsx`

Add the MyJobs route. Add lazy import at top:
```tsx
const MyJobs = lazy(() => import("./pages/MyJobs"));
```

Add route (protected):
```tsx
<Route path="/jobs" element={<ProtectedRoute><MyJobs /></ProtectedRoute>} />
```

### 3. Modify `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Rankora/src/pages/Index.tsx`

**Dashboard changes:**
- Remove the `JobsOverviewCard` import and usage
- Replace it with a simple "Recent Jobs" section showing max 5 recent jobs as clean cards
- Add a "View All Jobs →" link that navigates to `/jobs`
- Keep: Stats cards, Create Job button, Getting Started guide (show only when pastJobs.length === 0)
- Add URL param handling: on mount, check for `?job=xxx` and auto-load that job, check for `?new=1` and go to new job view

For the Recent Jobs section, use simple cards (NOT the full table):
```tsx
{/* Recent Jobs */}
{pastJobs.length > 0 && (
  <div className="space-y-3">
    <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
      <h2 className="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">Recent Jobs</h2>
      <Link to="/jobs" className="text-xs font-medium text-primary hover:text-primary/80 transition-colors">
        View All Jobs →
      </Link>
    </div>
    <div className="grid gap-3">
      {pastJobs.slice(0, 5).map((job) => (
        <Card key={job.id} className="cursor-pointer hover:shadow-md transition-all border border-border/60" onClick={() => loadJobData(job.id)}>
          <CardContent className="px-5 py-3.5 flex items-center justify-between">
            <div className="flex items-center gap-3 min-w-0">
              <div className="h-9 w-9 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
                <Briefcase className="h-4 w-4 text-primary" />
              </div>
              <div className="min-w-0">
                <p className="text-sm font-medium text-foreground truncate">{job.title || "Untitled Job"}</p>
                <p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-0.5">
                  {job.resume_count} resume{job.resume_count !== 1 ? "s" : ""} · {format(new Date(job.created_at), "MMM d, yyyy")}
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div className="flex items-center gap-3 shrink-0">
              <Badge variant={job.status === "completed" ? "success" : job.status === "pending" ? "warning" : "outline"} className="text-xs">
                {job.status.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + job.status.slice(1)}
              </Badge>
              <ChevronRight className="h-4 w-4 text-muted-foreground" />
            </div>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
)}
```

Add these imports to Index.tsx:
- `import { Link, useSearchParams } from "react-router-dom";`
- `import { Badge } from "@/components/ui/badge";`
- `import { ChevronRight } from "lucide-react";` (add to existing lucide import)
- `import { format } from "date-fns";`
- Remove: `import JobsOverviewCard from "@/components/JobsOverviewCard";`

Add URL param handling in the component:
```tsx
const [searchParams, setSearchParams] = useSearchParams();

// Handle URL params for deep linking from My Jobs page
useEffect(() => {
  const jobParam = searchParams.get("job");
  const newParam = searchParams.get("new");

  if (jobParam && user) {
    loadJobData(jobParam);
    setSearchParams({}, { replace: true });
  } else if (newParam) {
    handleNewJob();
    setSearchParams({}, { replace: true });
  }
}, [searchParams, user]);
```

IMPORTANT: The `useSearchParams` needs to be within a Router context which it already is.

### 4. Modify `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Rankora/src/components/JobSidebar.tsx`

Add "My Jobs" nav item in the HOME section, between Dashboard and the separator:

In the SidebarMenu inside the HOME section, after the Dashboard SidebarMenuItem, add:

```tsx
{isAuthenticated && (
  <SidebarMenuItem>
    <SidebarMenuButton onClick={() => navigate("/jobs")}>
      <Briefcase className="h-4 w-4" />
      <span>My Jobs</span>
    </SidebarMenuButton>
  </SidebarMenuItem>
)}
```

Add `useNavigate` import from react-router-dom and use it in the component. Also add the Briefcase icon (already imported).

Also, add `import { useNavigate } from "react-router-dom";` and `const navigate = useNavigate();` in the component.

### 5. Show Getting Started guide ONLY for new users

In Index.tsx, only show the Getting Started card when `pastJobs.length === 0` and `!loadingPastJobs`:
```tsx
{pastJobs.length === 0 && !loadingPastJobs && (
  <Card>...</Card>
)}
```

## IMPORTANT
- Run `npm run build` after all changes to verify zero type errors
- Do NOT modify types.ts
- Keep all existing error handling
- The `PastJob` interface export from Index.tsx must stay (MyJobs imports it)

